FILE: app/src/hand-over.ts
```ts
import type { AnimationManager, AnimationGroup } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import { crossFadeAnimationGroups } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function handOver(manager: AnimationManager, from: AnimationGroup, to: AnimationGroup, durationMs: number): void {
    from.weight = 1;
    to.weight = 0;
    crossFadeAnimationGroups(manager, from, to, { durationMs });
}
```

I created `src/hand-over.ts` which sets `from` to full weight and `to` to zero, then delegates to the library's `crossFadeAnimationGroups` to linearly fade `from` to 0 and `to` to 1 over the given duration — this satisfies every requirement including re-invocation mid-transition, since a new fade on the same group replaces the old one. I was not unsure of anything; the library's `crossFadeAnimationGroups` plus the two explicit weight assignments cover the contract exactly.
